cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Terminal multiplexers (SDS.OSV1-USE1.7)"
message: >-
  If you use this training module, please cite it using the
  metadata from this file.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Ovidiu
    family-names: Pescar
    email: ovidiupescar@gmail.com
    affiliation: Fisherman Engineering
repository-code: "https://github.com/ovidiupescar/evita-terminal-multiplexers"
abstract: >-
  EVITA training module for course SDS.OSV1 (Virtualization and the
  Linux operating system), module USE1.7: what a terminal multiplexer
  is for, and how to use one. A tmux server on the remote machine owns
  the session, so a command survives a dropped connection; windows and
  panes give several views inside one connection; and an editor running
  in a session can be left mid-edit and picked up again. Four episodes
  with executed console evidence and 52 captured terminal screens, five
  staged failures (a session ended by exit, the nesting refusal, an
  attach with no server, a killed pane, and a session killed while a
  Vim buffer was unwritten), a GNU Screen section for systems without
  tmux, and a summative quiz with a hands-on task; baseline Ubuntu
  24.04 LTS, tmux 3.4, GNU Screen 4.09.01, ordinary user account.
